        "num_ratings": 6,
        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Tough for a 2 credit class, even Dr. Winterstein said it would be more like 3. But that aside, I absolutely loved the class. Dr. W is such a great guy! Funny, engaging, and cares more about student's progress and learning than actual assignments. One of my favorite professors to date. Definitely recommend, but don't assume it's easy 2 credits.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Class meets once a week and on top of that you are expected to take part in online lectures/modules. Lots of studying required for exams-especially if you have no prior background in anatomy. Lots of work and tough for a two credit class. Dr. Winterstein is great; funny, interesting, and knows his stuff for sure.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Dr. Winterstein is one of the best professors I've had.  Very funny and nice guy. I have had him for Kines 127 and 227 and both consisted of all multiple choice exams.  The finals were not cumulative.  You will not regret taking a class taught by Dr. W.",
                "difficulty_rating": 1,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Dr. W is funny, passionate about Athletic Training, and interesting to listen to.  Great introduction class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Best professor ever. Seriously take one of his classes you won't regret it. Super funny and nice. Cares about his students. Overall a great guy and wonderful professor.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Class isn't too bad as long as you follow along with the readings and pay attention to the lectures. Dr. Winterstein is very funny and the combination of him and Patrick is perfect!",
